---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const services = [
  'Interior painting: walls, ceilings, trim, and doors',
  'Exterior painting: siding, trim, and fascia',
  'Cabinet refinishing',
  'Drywall repair and surface prep',
  'Deck and fence staining',
  'Color consultation',
];

const beyondPaint = [
  'Siding repair and replacement',
  'Deck building and repair',
  'Window and door replacement',
  'Trim and finish carpentry',
  'Kitchen and bathroom remodels',
  'Tile installation',
];
---
<Base title="Services">
  <article class="services">
    <p class="eyebrow">What We Do</p>
    <h1>Painting Services</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        We work with homeowners across the Eastside, from a single room that needs a fresh coat
        to a whole-house exterior or a full remodel. Painting is the heart of what we do, and the
        trades around it are where we really shine.
      </p>
      <p>
        We're a family business, and every job is done by us: no subcontractors, no rotating
        crews. We're licensed, bonded, and insured, we use quality materials, and we leave your
        home clean at the end of every day.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section>
      <h2>Our Services</h2>
      <h3>Painting</h3>
      <ul class="service-list">
        {services.map((service) => <li>{service}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <h3>Beyond Paint</h3>
      <ul class="service-list">
        {beyondPaint.map((service) => <li>{service}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p class="note">
        For electrical and plumbing, we're happy to recommend contractors we trust. You hire them
        directly, with no markup from us.
      </p>
    </section>

    <figure class="banner">
      <img
        src="/images/projects/newcastle_mudroom/siding_over_insulation.jpg"
        alt="A mudroom addition in progress, with new yellow lap siding going up over house wrap and insulation"
      />
      <figcaption>Prep · Build · Paint</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Our Process</h2>
      <p>
        Every project starts with a free estimate. We'll visit your home, walk through what you
        have in mind, take measurements, and point out anything we notice, like rot, peeling, or
        water damage, that should be handled first. Then we'll send you a clear written quote.
      </p>
      <p>
        Once the work starts, prep comes first. We wash, scrape, sand, patch, caulk, and prime
        until every surface is ready, and we choose paints and materials suited to each surface
        and to Pacific Northwest weather. That groundwork is what keeps a finish looking good for
        years instead of seasons.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>What to Expect</h2>
      <p>
        Since you're working with the owners directly, you'll always know who to call. We'll keep
        you posted from the first visit to the final walkthrough.
      </p>

      <h3>Before We Start</h3>
      <p>
        We'll help you choose colors and finishes and settle on a schedule that works for you.
        On the first day, we move and cover furniture and protect floors, fixtures, and
        landscaping before any work begins.
      </p>

      <h3>During the Project</h3>
      <p>
        We keep regular working hours and let you know what's planned for each day. If we find
        something unexpected, we'll talk it through with you before going further. At the end of
        each day, we clean up and leave your home livable.
      </p>

      <h3>After We Finish</h3>
      <p>
        We'll do a final walkthrough together and take care of any touch-ups on the spot. We
        leave labeled leftover paint for future touch-ups, and if something isn't right down the
        road, give us a call.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="cta">
      <h2>Ready to get started?</h2>
      <p>Tell us about your project and we'll schedule a free estimate.</p>
      <a class="button" href="/contact/">Request an Estimate</a>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .services {
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 3rem 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1.6rem;
  }
  h3 {
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }
  .service-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(18rem, 1fr));
    gap: 0.75rem 2rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .service-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
  }
  .service-list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.55em;
    left: 0;
    width: 0.5rem;
    height: 0.5rem;
    background: var(--brand);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }
  .note {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .banner {
    margin: 3rem 0 0;
  }
  .banner img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 21 / 9;
    object-fit: cover;
    background: var(--line);
    border-radius: 14px;
  }
  .banner figcaption {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--brand);
  }
  .cta {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
    padding: 2.5rem 2rem;
    text-align: center;
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 14px;
  }
  .cta h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .cta p {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .banner img {
      aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    }
  }
</style>
